   "number": "111",
   "text": "In this Part, “contaminated site” means an area of land in which the soil, including any groundwater lying beneath it, or the water including the sediment and bed below it, contains a contaminant which is in an amount, concentration, or level in excess of that prescribed by regulation or allowed under a permit. « lieu pollué » “land” in section 114 to 117 does not include land the right to the beneficial use and proceeds of which remains with the government of Canada; « terrain » “responsible party” means the person who had possession, charge or control of the contaminant at the time of its release into the natural environment; « partie responsable »",
